.TH "SLIPWAY-DESCRIBE" "1" "" "slipway 0.1.0" "Slipway Manual"
.SH NAME
slipway\-describe \- Show details of one or many resources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "slipway describe"
.I "(TYPE [NAME...] | TYPE/NAME...)"\&
.RI [ flags ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show details of one or many resources.
.PP
Print a detailed description of the selected resources, including the state of the repository at the registered path and where it differs from the manifest. You may select a single object by name, all objects of that type, or use a label selector.
.PP
Resource types: projects (project, proj) and groups (group). Type words are case\-insensitive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-selector\fR \fIEXPR\fR
Selector (label query) to filter on, supports '=', '==', '!=', 'in', 'notin' (e.g. \-l key1=value1,key2=value2,key3 in (value3)). Matching objects must satisfy all of the specified label constraints.
.TP
\fB\-\-field\-selector\fR \fIEXPR\fR
Selector (field query) to filter on, supports '=', '==', and '!=' (e.g. \-\-field\-selector key1=value1,key2=value2). Projects support metadata.name, metadata.group, spec.path, status.state, status.branch, status.lastFetch; groups support metadata.name. status.lastFetch is never for a project with no fetch on record.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-all\-groups\fR
If present, list the requested object(s) across all groups. The group in the current configuration is ignored even if specified with \-\-group.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# Describe a project
slipway describe project hldr
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Describe every project in the work group
slipway describe projects \-n work
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Describe the projects labeled lang=rust
slipway describe projects \-l lang=rust
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Describe the projects on the main branch
slipway describe projects \-\-field\-selector status.branch=main
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Describe a group
slipway describe group work
.EE
